From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] catalystwan: log out of vManage when a module exits

MEASURED on a live vManage 20.7.1. Upstream never logs out: every module
invocation opens a ManagerSession and exits through exit_json/fail_json without
closing it, so each call LEAKS a server-side session until vManage's idle
timeout.

vManage caps concurrent sessions per user, and once the cap is hit it answers
every new login with

    429 Client Error: Too Many Requests for url: .../dataservice/client/server

which persisted for more than an hour after the calls stopped. A readiness loop
of ~100 module calls locked the whole lane out of the very appliance it was
waiting for -- and the symptom (429 on login) looks like a credential or
rate-limit problem rather than a leak, which is what made it expensive to find.

The SDK's own close() docstring says to use the session as a context manager;
this is the equivalent for a module that exits through exit_json/fail_json.
close() logs out first (ManagerSession.close -> logout -> super().close()).

Best-effort by construction: a failure to log out must never mask the module's
real result, so the close is wrapped and its exception swallowed. _session is
cleared before closing so a double exit cannot double-close.

UPSTREAM ASK: FILE. Session leakage affects every consumer of this collection,
not just us.

---
diff --git a/plugins/module_utils/vmanage_module.py b/plugins/module_utils/vmanage_module.py
index c2f1d66..0185ef9 100644
--- a/plugins/module_utils/vmanage_module.py
+++ b/plugins/module_utils/vmanage_module.py
@@ -91,10 +91,37 @@ class AnsibleCatalystwanModule:
 
         self._session = None
 
+    def _close_session(self) -> None:
+        # SKYFORGE FIX (2026-09-02, measured on vManage 20.7.1). Upstream never
+        # logs out: every module invocation opens a ManagerSession and exits
+        # without closing it, so each call LEAKS a server-side session until
+        # vManage's idle timeout. vManage caps concurrent sessions per user and,
+        # once the cap is hit, answers every new login with
+        #
+        #   429 Client Error: Too Many Requests for url: .../dataservice/client/server
+        #
+        # which persisted for more than an hour after the calls stopped -- a
+        # readiness loop of ~100 module calls locked the whole lane out of the
+        # appliance it was waiting for. The SDK's own docstring on close() says
+        # to use the session as a context manager; this is the equivalent for a
+        # module that exits through exit_json/fail_json. close() logs out first
+        # (ManagerSession.close -> logout -> super().close()). Best-effort: a
+        # failure to log out must never mask the module's real result.
+        session = self._session
+        self._session = None
+        if session is None:
+            return
+        try:
+            session.close()
+        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - logout is best-effort by design
+            pass
+
     def exit_json(self, **kwargs):
+        self._close_session()
         self.module.exit_json(**kwargs)
 
     def fail_json(self, msg: str, **kwargs):
+        self._close_session()
         self.module.fail_json(msg, **kwargs)
 
     @property

